1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,110
The Meredith family lived in a small community.
梅雷迪思一家住在一个小社区里。

2
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:09,380
As the economy was in decline, some people in the town had lost their jobs.
由于经济衰退，镇上有些人丢了工作。

3
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:13,150
Many of their families were struggling to make ends meet.
他们中很多人的家里都在艰难度日，勉强维持生计。

4
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:16,540
People were trying to help each other meet the challenges.
人们都在设法互相帮助，共渡难关。

5
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,190
Mrs. Meredith was a most kind and thoughtful woman.
梅雷迪思太太是一位非常善良、体贴的女士。

6
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:23,200
She spent a great deal of time visiting the poor.
她花了大量时间去探望穷人。

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,440
She knew they had problems, and they needed all kinds of help.
她知道他们有困难，需要各种各样的帮助。

8
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:31,560
When she had time, she would bring food and medicine to them.
她一有空，就会给他们送去食物和药品。

9
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:36,930
One morning she told her children about a family she had visited the day before.
一天早上，她跟孩子们讲起了她前一天探望过的一户人家。

10
00:00:37,730 --> 00:00:43,755
There was a man sick in bed, his wife, who took care of him and could not go out to work, and their little boy.
这家有一个卧病在床的男人，他的妻子要照顾他，没法出去工作，还有他们的小儿子。

11
00:00:44,555 --> 00:00:48,945
The little boy—his name was Bernard—had interested her very much.
那个小男孩名叫伯纳德，让她很感兴趣。

12
00:00:49,745 --> 00:00:54,065
“I wish you could see him,” she said to her own children, John, Harry, and Clara.
“真希望你们能见见他。”她对自己的孩子约翰、哈里和克拉拉说。

13
00:00:54,865 --> 00:00:56,465
“He is such a help to his mother.
“他可真是妈妈的好帮手。

14
00:00:57,265 --> 00:01:00,905
He wants very much to earn some money, but I don’t see what he can do.”
他非常想挣点钱，可我看不出他能做什么。”

15
00:01:01,705 --> 00:01:05,635
After their mother left the room, the children sat thinking about Bernard.
妈妈离开房间后，孩子们坐在那里想着伯纳德的事。

16
00:01:06,435 --> 00:01:08,925
“I wish we could help him to earn money,” said Clara.
“真希望我们能帮他挣到钱。”克拉拉说。

17
00:01:09,725 --> 00:01:11,605
“His family is suffering so much.”
“他家日子太苦了。”

18
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,515
“So do I,” said Harry.
“我也这么想。”哈里说。

19
00:01:14,315 --> 00:01:16,295
“We really should do something to assist them.”
“我们真该做点什么来帮帮他们。”

20
00:01:17,095 --> 00:01:24,055
For some moments, John said nothing, but, suddenly, he sprang to his feet and cried, “I have a great idea!
约翰好一会儿都没说话，可突然，他一下子跳起来，喊道：“我有个好主意！

21
00:01:24,855 --> 00:01:27,415
I have a solution that we can all help accomplish.”
我有个办法，咱们都能出份力，帮着把这事办成。”

22
00:01:28,215 --> 00:01:31,275
The other children also jumped up, all attention.
其他孩子也跳了起来，全神贯注地听着。

23
00:01:32,075 --> 00:01:35,025
When John had an idea, it was sure to be a good one.
约翰一有主意，那准是个好主意。

24
00:01:35,825 --> 00:01:37,635
“I tell you what we can do,” said John.
“我来告诉你们咱们能做什么。”约翰说。

25
00:01:38,435 --> 00:01:41,155
“You know that big box of corn Uncle John sent us?
“还记得约翰叔叔寄给我们的那一大箱玉米吗？

26
00:01:41,955 --> 00:01:48,275
Well, we can make popcorn, and put it into paper bags, and Bernard can take it around to the houses and sell it.”
嗯，我们可以做爆米花，装进纸袋，让伯纳德挨家挨户去卖。”

27
00:01:49,075 --> 00:01:53,175
When Mrs. Meredith heard of John’s idea, she thought it was a good one, too.
梅雷迪思太太听说了约翰的主意，也觉得很好。

28
00:01:53,975 --> 00:01:57,593
With everything ready, Bernard started out on his new business.
一切准备就绪，伯纳德开始了他的新生意。
